# Supermarket distribution (WIP, BASED OFF CLOTHING SHOPS - ClothesShop1990 = 100 distweight)
#
# https://publications.gc.ca/collections/Collection-R/Statcan/63-210-XIB/0009863-210-XIB.pdf
# https://publications.gc.ca/collections/collection_2018/statcan/63-210/CS63-210-1978.pdf
# StatsCan reports for 1978 and 1998 giving floor areas for supermarkets ('combination grocery stores' in 1978)
#
# https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a7f0f7740f0b62305b84d2e/Domestic_Food_Consumption_and_Expenditure_1970_and_1971.pdf
# UK gov. report for total food consumption, 1970 (use as reference for Supermarket1960 consumption)
# https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20130103031008mp_/http://www.defra.gov.uk/statistics/files/defra-stats-food-family-annual-2002.pdf
# UK gov. report for total food consumption, 2002 (use as reference for Supermarket1980 consumption)
#
# of note: since Supermarket1960 is present in modern day, calculations take this into account
# Comparing Canadian figures for supermarket floor area in 1998 and 1978 to clothing store floor area for the same returns:
# Supermarket1960 = 14 (for ClothingStore1960 = 40)
# Supermarket1980 = 40 (for ClothingStore1980 = 100)
# for Supermarket1950, we use 'general stores' in 1978 to get average floor area of 14433 ft2 -> 1340 m2 -> 11.66 stores/tile
# Then refer to StatsCan Retail Chain Stores, 1962, for overall store count & compare with clothing store count
# -> 146 general stores in Canada in 1962 -> 2,107,218 ft2 total
# Compare to clothing stores - in 1978 avg square footage of 10,188,621 for 2723 stores -> avg 3741 ft2/store
# In 1962, 1297 stores * 3741 ft2 = 4,852,077 ft2
# = 2107218/4852077 = 0.434 ratio of tiles in-game of Supermarket1950 to ClothesStore1945
# ClothesStore1945 dist weight of 20 -> Supermarket1950 dist weight of 8.68 -> round to 9
# 
# TODO: Add calculations later showing work for Supermarket1960 + Supermarket1980

Obj=factory
Name=Supermarket1950
# 1950 supermarket (1x1 convenience store)
population_and_visitor_demand_capacity=324
employment_capacity=110
mail_demand=24
